Title: an agent rides out a model-endpoint outage (and a mid-run 401) instead of failing
Why: a ~5-minute staging endpoint stall ending in one 401 killed a two-hour eval scan at 34 min; upstream replays a transient error only 5 times over ~1 min and never a 401. The Jitera-profile rider (strix/jitera/resilience.py) keeps replaying outage-shaped failures for up to 15 minutes per incident
Upstream-PR: none

